From b869aaa8af390b364d56050127503237c45cdb91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:10:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Blocks step back and put the blade in the blow's path;
 fingers hold weapons

- combat: a blocked blow drives the guard back a real step (root motion
  over 0.3 s, length 0.18 m + 0.07 m per m/s of knockback, max 0.6 m)
  instead of only a slide.
- block.rs: while guarding, the weapon hand moves so the blade crosses
  the incoming swing between the fighters, at the attacker's blade
  height and on its side, ramping in before the active frames.
- combat::arm sets HeldGrip (handle cylinder in the hand frame), which
  select forwards to the hand rig, so fingers close on the weapon.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017RTuqxaQfwuvFPEJrcXYEk
